{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaWordSelection","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Notation","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":47,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmit_vertex_not_psdFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmit_vertex_not_psdFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L389-L394","doc":"**The concrete `H₃` vertex is not PSD-feasible for any `0 < q ≠ 1`.** No\nhypothesis on `b` remains: it is the Hoefsmit value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmit_std_sigma0_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmit_std_sigma0_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":378,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L378-L387","doc":"The `σ₀` matrix satisfies the Hecke relation too (its entries are the two\neigenvalues). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmit_std_sigma1_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmit_std_sigma1_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L358-L376","doc":"**The Hoefsmit `σ₁` satisfies the Hecke relation `σ₁² = h·σ₁ + 1`** — a wrong\n`a`, `a'` or `b` fails this. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitB_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitB_sq","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L351-L356","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitB_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitB_pos","kind":"theorem","line":344,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L344-L349","doc":"**`b > 0` for every `0 < q ≠ 1`** — the `(2,1)` block is irreducible and the\nhypothesis of `vertex_not_psdFeasible` is met by the actual Hoefsmit data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.qThree_div_qTwo_sq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.qThree_div_qTwo_sq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L341-L342","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitA_mul_A'_add_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitA_mul_A'_add_one","kind":"theorem","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L327-L339","doc":"`a·a' + 1 = [3]_q / [2]_q²` — so the Hoefsmit `b²` is a ratio of quantum\nintegers, independent of the square root's sign convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitA_add_A'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitA_add_A'","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L315-L325","doc":"`a + a' = h`: the two diagonal entries sum to the trace `q − q⁻¹` of `σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.one_sub_pow_four_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.one_sub_pow_four_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":307,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L307-L313","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitB","kind":"def","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L304-L305","doc":"`b = √(a·a' + 1)`, the Hoefsmit off-diagonal entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.qThree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.qThree","kind":"def","line":301,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L301-L302","doc":"`[3]_q = q² + 1 + q⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.qTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.qTwo","kind":"def","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L298-L299","doc":"`[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitA'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitA'","kind":"def","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L295-L296","doc":"`a' = h/(1 − q⁻⁴)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitA","kind":"def","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L291-L293","doc":"`a = h/(1 − q⁴)` (content distance `ρ = −2` for the swap `(2 3)` on the\ntableau `[[1,2],[3]]`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hOf","kind":"def","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L288-L289","doc":"`h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.sdpSelected_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.sdpSelected_nil","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L271-L279","doc":"**What the literal `SDPSelected` selects on `H₃` with the crossing-count\ncost**: the empty word, whenever it is a candidate. The non-zero selection is\nthe probe's question (owner ruling 2026-08-30: minimal *non-zero* feasible). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.vertex_not_psdFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.vertex_not_psdFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L263-L269","doc":"Hence a single vertex `σ₀σ₁⁻¹` is **not** PSD-feasible on `H₃` — the\n`(2,1)` block fails the Hermitian half of `Matrix.PosSemidef`. Mirror of\nstep 1's `h2_two_feasible_one_not` (`σ₀` infeasible on `H₂`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.vertex_std_not_isHermitian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.vertex_std_not_isHermitian","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L246-L261","doc":"**The `(2,1)` image of one pair-production vertex is not symmetric** when the\nblock is irreducible (`b ≠ 0`): its off-diagonal entries are `q·b` and\n`−q⁻¹·b`, equal only if `b·(q + q⁻¹) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.nil_psdFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.nil_psdFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L240-L244","doc":"The empty word (the identity of `H₃`) is PSD-feasible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.psdFeasible_iff_std","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.psdFeasible_iff_std","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L220-L238","doc":"**For a γγ-word, PSD feasibility is decided by the `(2,1)` block alone**:\nthe `(3)` and `(1³)` images are both the `1×1` matrix `1`, which is PSD. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.h3Blocks","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.h3Blocks","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L210-L218","doc":"**`H₃` Wedderburn block data on words**: `(3)` by the trivial character,\n`(2,1)` by the Hoefsmit image with generator matrices `S`, `(1³)` by the\nalternating character. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.H3Block.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.H3Block.dim","kind":"def","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L204-L208","doc":"Their dimensions `1, 2, 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.instDecidableEqH3Block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.instDecidableEqH3Block","kind":"instance","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L202-L202","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.H3Block.sgn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.H3Block.sgn","kind":"ctor","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L201-L201","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.H3Block.std","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.H3Block.std","kind":"ctor","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L200-L200","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.H3Block.triv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.H3Block.triv","kind":"ctor","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L199-L199","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.H3Block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.H3Block","kind":"inductive","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L197-L202","doc":"The three Wedderburn blocks of `H₃(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.stdImage_vertex_entries","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.stdImage_vertex_entries","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L181-L189","doc":"The `(2,1)` image of the pair-production vertex, entrywise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitGen","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L175-L179","doc":"The two generator matrices as a function of the generator index (only\n`0` and `1` occur in an `H₃` word). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitSigma1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitSigma1","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L172-L173","doc":"Hoefsmit orthogonal form of `σ₁` on `(2,1)`: the symmetric `[[a, b], [b, a']]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitSigma0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.hoefsmitSigma0","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L169-L170","doc":"Hoefsmit orthogonal form of `σ₀` on `(2,1)`: `diag(q, −q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.stdImage_vertex_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.stdImage_vertex_zero","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L165-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.stdImage_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.stdImage_nil","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L162-L163","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.stdImage","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.stdImage","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L156-L160","doc":"Left-to-right product of the crossing images: the `(2,1)`-block image of a\nword. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.crossingImage","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.crossingImage","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L150-L154","doc":"Image of one crossing under generator matrices `S 0 = ρ(σ₀)`, `S 1 = ρ(σ₁)`,\nwith `σᵢ⁻¹ ↦ ρ(σᵢ) − h·1` (the Hecke relation `σ² = hσ + 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.trivChar_single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.trivChar_single","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L137-L140","doc":"A single positive crossing has trivial character `q` (it is not a unit of\nthe character, so `q ≠ 1` distinguishes it from every γγ-word). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.trivChar_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.trivChar_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L130-L135","doc":"**The `(3)`-block image of every γγ-produced word is `1`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.trivChar_vertex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.trivChar_vertex","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L127-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.trivChar_append","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.trivChar_append","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L123-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.trivChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.trivChar","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L117-L121","doc":"The one-dimensional **trivial** representation `σᵢ ↦ q` (so `σᵢ⁻¹ ↦ q⁻¹`),\nevaluated on a word: the `(3)` block of `H₃(q)`, and the `(n)` block of any\n`Hₙ(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.gammaGamma_inH3_eq_vertexPow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.gammaGamma_inH3_eq_vertexPow","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L96-L109","doc":"**Inside `H₃`, every γγ-produced word is a vertex power.** A vertex\n`σᵢσᵢ₊₁⁻¹` uses generator `i + 1`, so `i + 1 ≤ 1` forces `i = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.inH3_vertexPow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.inH3_vertexPow","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L85-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.InH3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.InH3","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L82-L83","doc":"A word lies in `H₃` iff it uses only the generators `σ₀, σ₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.vertexPow_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.vertexPow_length","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L77-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.vertexPow_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.vertexPow_three","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L75-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.vertexPow_gammaGamma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.vertexPow_gammaGamma","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L70-L73","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.vertexPow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaSelectorH3.vertexPow","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaSelectorH3.lean#L64-L68","doc":"`(σ₀σ₁⁻¹)^k`, as the nested product the `GammaGammaWord` constructors\nproduce (`vertexPow 3 = borromean`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}